  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc. The evidence strongly supports this architecture: scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder, multiprofile adds ~13% over single profile, transformer aggregation is marginally best, and multimodal fusion adds ~3.5% over RNA-only. The key remaining uncertainty within this top-performing family is the fusion strategy: concat vs. weighted. Config_033 is an exact single-variable comparison to config_032 (only fusion changes from concat to weighted), cleanly isolating whether learned or adaptive weighting of the two modalities outperform simple concatenation. With only 2 experiments left, this focused exploitation of the best-known architecture while resolving the fusion question is the highest-value next step. If weighted wins, the final experiment can push further (e.g., a better image encoder); if concat holds, we confirm the current best and can spend the last experiment on a different axis."
}

